{"abstract":[{"text":"Calculate the positions of celestial bodies in various coordinate systems.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"AstronomyKit"}],"title":"Celestial Positions","roleHeading":"Article"},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/CelestialPositions","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"AstronomyKit can calculate positions for the Sun, Moon, planets, Jupiter’s moons, and fixed stars. Positions can be expressed in multiple coordinate systems.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Celestial-Bodies","level":2,"text":"Celestial Bodies","type":"heading"},{"anchor":"Available-Bodies","level":3,"text":"Available Bodies","type":"heading"},{"code":["\/\/ Major bodies","let sun = CelestialBody.sun","let moon = CelestialBody.moon","let mars = CelestialBody.mars","","\/\/ Major planets other than Earth (Mercury through Neptune)","for planet in CelestialBody.planets {","    print(planet.name)","}","","\/\/ Jupiter's Galilean moons","for moon in CelestialBody.galileanMoons {","    print(moon.name)  \/\/ Io, Europa, Ganymede, Callisto","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Body-Properties","level":3,"text":"Body Properties","type":"heading"},{"code":["let mars = CelestialBody.mars","","print(mars.name)           \/\/ \"Mars\"","print(mars.orbitalPeriod)  \/\/ ~686 days","print(mars.massProduct)    \/\/ Mass × G in AU³\/day²","print(mars.isPlanet)       \/\/ true","print(mars.isNakedEyeVisible)  \/\/ true"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Looking-Up-Bodies-by-Name","level":3,"text":"Looking Up Bodies by Name","type":"heading"},{"code":["if let body = CelestialBody(name: \"Jupiter\") {","    print(\"Found: \\(body)\")","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Horizon-Coordinates","level":2,"text":"Horizon Coordinates","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Where does a body appear in your local sky?","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let observer = Observer(latitude: 40.7128, longitude: -74.0060)","let mars = try CelestialBody.mars.horizon(at: .now, from: observer)","","print(\"Altitude: \\(mars.altitude)°\")     \/\/ Height above horizon","print(\"Azimuth: \\(mars.azimuth)°\")       \/\/ Compass bearing","print(\"Direction: \\(mars.compassDirection)\")  \/\/ N, NE, E, SE, etc.","","if mars.isAboveHorizon {","    print(\"Mars is visible!\")","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Equatorial-Coordinates","level":2,"text":"Equatorial Coordinates","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Right ascension and declination on the celestial sphere:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let eq = try CelestialBody.saturn.equatorial(at: .now)","","print(\"RA: \\(eq.rightAscension) hours\")","print(\"Dec: \\(eq.declination)°\")","print(\"Distance: \\(eq.distance) AU\")","","\/\/ Formatted output","print(eq.rightAscensionFormatted)   \/\/ \"02h 15m 30.2s\"","print(eq.declinationFormatted)      \/\/ \"+12° 34' 56.7\"\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Equator-Date-Options","level":3,"text":"Equator Date Options","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Choose the reference equinox:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let body = CelestialBody.mars","","\/\/ J2000 coordinates (default) - standard reference epoch","let j2000 = try body.equatorial(at: .now, equatorDate: .j2000)","","\/\/ Coordinates of the observation date - accounts for precession","let ofDate = try body.equatorial(at: .now, equatorDate: .ofDate)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Ecliptic-Coordinates-and-Velocity","level":2,"text":"Ecliptic Coordinates and Velocity","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Position and rate of change relative to the true ecliptic and equinox of date:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let longitude = try CelestialBody.venus.eclipticLongitude(at: .now)","print(\"Venus ecliptic longitude: \\(longitude)°\")","","\/\/ Sun's full ecliptic position","let sunPos = try Sun.position(at: .now)","print(\"Sun: λ=\\(sunPos.longitude)°, β=\\(sunPos.latitude)°\")","","\/\/ Position and velocity together via EclipticState","let state = try CelestialBody.mars.geocentricEclipticState(at: .now)","print(\"Mars λ=\\(state.longitude)°, dλ\/dt=\\(state.longitudeRate)°\/day\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/EclipticState","isActive":true},{"text":" provides ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"longitudeRate"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"latitudeRate"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distanceRate"},{"text":" per Terrestrial Time day via ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/CelestialBody\/geocentricEclipticState(at:aberration:)","isActive":true},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Sun\/eclipticState(at:)","isActive":true},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Moon\/eclipticState(at:)","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Position-Vectors","level":2,"text":"Position Vectors","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Cartesian coordinates in 3D space:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ Geocentric (from Earth's center)","let geo = try CelestialBody.jupiter.geocentricPosition(at: .now)","print(\"Distance from Earth: \\(geo.magnitude) AU\")","","\/\/ Heliocentric (from Sun's center)","let helio = try CelestialBody.mars.heliocentricPosition(at: .now)","print(\"Distance from Sun: \\(helio.magnitude) AU\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Distance-Calculations","level":2,"text":"Distance Calculations","type":"heading"},{"code":["\/\/ Distance from Sun","let auFromSun = try CelestialBody.mars.distanceFromSun(at: .now)","print(\"Mars is \\(auFromSun) AU from the Sun\")","","\/\/ Angular separation from Sun","let angle = try CelestialBody.venus.angleFromSun(at: .now)","print(\"Venus is \\(angle)° from the Sun\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Constellation-Identification","level":2,"text":"Constellation Identification","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Find which constellation contains a body:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let constellation = try CelestialBody.mars.constellation(at: .now)","print(\"\\(constellation.symbol) - \\(constellation.name)\")","\/\/ Output: \"Tau - Taurus\"","","\/\/ Or from raw coordinates","let orion = try Constellation.find(rightAscension: 5.9195, declination: 7.4071)","print(orion.name)  \/\/ \"Orion\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Fixed-Stars","level":2,"text":"Fixed Stars","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Define and track fixed stars by their J2000 catalog coordinates using ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/FixedStar","isActive":true},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ Define Algol (Beta Persei)","let algol = FixedStar(","    name: \"Algol\",","    rightAscension: 3.136148,  \/\/ J2000 RA in hours","    declination: 40.9556,      \/\/ J2000 Dec in degrees","    distance: 92.95    \/\/ Light-years",")","","\/\/ Get ecliptic longitude (true ecliptic and equinox of date, same frame as the planets)","let longitude = try algol.eclipticLongitude(at: .now)","","\/\/ Get position in local sky","let observer = Observer(latitude: 40.7, longitude: -74.0)","let horizon = try algol.horizon(at: .now, from: observer)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"J2000 coordinates can be found from star catalogs like SIMBAD, Hipparcos, or the Yale Bright Star Catalog.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Aberration-Correction","level":2,"text":"Aberration Correction","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Control light-time and aberration corrections:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let body = CelestialBody.mars","","\/\/ With correction (default) - apparent position","let apparent = try body.geocentricPosition(at: .now, aberration: .corrected)","","\/\/ Without correction - geometric position","let geometric = try body.geocentricPosition(at: .now, aberration: .none)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Refraction-Correction","level":2,"text":"Refraction Correction","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Atmospheric refraction affects horizon coordinates:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let body = CelestialBody.mars","","\/\/ Normal refraction (default)","let normal = try body.horizon(at: .now, from: observer, refraction: .normal)","","\/\/ No refraction","let geometric = try body.horizon(at: .now, from: observer, refraction: .none)","","\/\/ JPL Horizons model","let jpl = try body.horizon(at: .now, from: observer, refraction: .jplHorizons)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/CoordinateSystems","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/CelestialBody","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Observer","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Constellation","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Aberration","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/EquatorDate"],"title":"Position Calculations","anchor":"Position-Calculations","generated":true}],"varian